    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that when an owner is created (and read back), the response include a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nI made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause the create and get endpoints both serialize owners through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the `displayName` is now present wherever an owner is returned. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreComputesDisplayName` check) is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
